{
  "manufacturer": "Yokogawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yokogawa",
  "model": "UTAdvanced UT75A digital indicating controller",
  "model_slug": "ut75a",
  "short_model": "UT75A",
  "aliases": [
    "UT75A"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (digital indicating temperature controller)",
  "applies_to": "Yokogawa UT75A one- or two-loop controller with RS-485 or Ethernet communication; D-register map from IM 05P07A01-01EN chapter 14.",
  "summary": "The UT75A is the high-end UTAdvanced PID controller with up to two loops, 20 SP groups and a simple program function. Its data live in D registers that map one-to-one onto Modbus holding registers over RS-485 (Modbus RTU/ASCII) or Modbus/TCP on Ethernet models. This map covers the process data block, the current SP/PID group for both loops and the operation-mode switches.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "ASCII",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The manual lists D register numbers (D2003). The Modbus reference number replaces the D with 4 (42003) and the wire address is that minus 40001, printed in the table's H No. column (D2003 = 07D2H)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "UTAdvanced Series Communication Interface (RS-485, Ethernet) User's Manual",
    "doc_number": "IM 05P07A01-01EN 13th Edition",
    "revision_date": "2026-03",
    "url": "https://web-material3.yokogawa.com/IM05P07A01-01EN.pdf",
    "pages": "D register addressing p. 3-4; D register classification p. 14-4; tables and descriptions pp. 14-6 to 14-20"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are 16-bit. Values are sent without their decimal point: PV/SP-type values follow the input's decimal point setting, percentages carry one decimal (scale 0.1).",
    "D2001-D2100 are read-only. D2101-D2112 / D2151-D2163 act on the SP group in use (1-20); D2114-D2135 / D2164-D2185 on the PID group in use (1-16 or R).",
    "Program-operation registers (D2031, D2327-D2329, pattern area D7701-D7900), ramp-rate registers D2112/D2113 and the GREEN-series compatible area (D0001-D2000) are not included.",
    "Only part of the D-register space is listed; alarm setpoints 5-8, cooling-side PID terms, SP/PID groups 9-20 (D9001 onward) and the setup parameter areas (D2501 onward) are left out.",
    "Modbus/TCP applies only to units with the Ethernet communication option."
  ],
